{"name":"Frozen Veins","hex":"#ecb3be","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"frozen","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having undergone the process of freezing; in ice form.","Immobilized."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["past participle of freeze"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frozen"},{"term":"veins","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of vein"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of vein"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/veins"}],"entries":[{"title":"Vein","blocks":[{"text":"A vein is a blood vessel in the circulatory system of humans and most other animals that carries blood towards the heart. Most veins carry deoxygenated blood from the tissues back to the heart; exceptions are those of the pulmonary and fetal circulations which carry oxygenated blood to the heart. In the systemic circulation, arteries carry oxygenated blood away from the heart, and veins return deoxygenated blood to the heart, in the deep veins."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Vein_%28retouched%29.svg/330px-Vein_%28retouched%29.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vein","wikidata":"Q9609"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Figure_40_03_07.jpg/500px-Figure_40_03_07.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Figure_40_03_07.jpg/500px-Figure_40_03_07.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Layers of vein wall shown in comparison to arterial wall","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFigure_40_03_07.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/2131_Major_Systematic_Veins.jpg/500px-2131_Major_Systematic_Veins.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedi